SM(224,{"n":"Genesis 3.9-24","a":"Fr Stephen De Young Archives/Genesis 3.9-24.mp3","d":3122.0,"s":[[0.24,"Come and study the Holy Scriptures with us as Father Stephen DeYoung teaches verse by verse on the podcast The Whole Counsel of God."],[8.96,"Father Stephen holds a PhD in biblical studies, and it's an Orthodox priest serving at Archangel Gabriel Orthodox Church in Lafayette, Louisiana."],[21.44,"So the Lord God called Adam and said to him, Adam, where are you?"],[25.76,"Now he's not doing this because he doesn't know."],[29.38,"He's doing this because he does know."],[35.67,"Verse 10, he replied, I heard your voice."],[38.55,"Oh, anyway, to finish that up."],[40.47,"That's where they're getting the voice of the Lord walking in the garden is from that word."],[46.39,"I heard your voice as you were walking in the garden, and I was afraid because I was naked, so I hid myself."],[54.35,"Um, not a good excuse if he's trying to cover up what he just did."],[59.48,"Because there's a bunch of immediate questions."],[61.72,"Why were you afraid?"],[63.88,"How'd you know you were naked?"],[66.28,"What made you think you could hide from God behind a tree?"],[71.22,"Like verse 11."],[77.14,"Thus he said, Who said you were naked?"],[80.02,"Have you eaten from the one tree from which I commanded you not to eat?"],[85.03,"So we have opportunities here to confess."],[89.91,"To fess up, to repent, to seek forgiveness."],[95.61,"Church and say, Yes, I did."],[97.41,"I was wrong."],[98.61,"Have mercy on me. etc"],[106.25,"Verse 12. Then Adam said, The woman you gave me gave me of the tree and I ate."],[111.29,"Wasn't me, it was this woman you put here with me."],[116.06,"Yes, it's really God's fault for putting the woman there."],[119.58,"But if not that, then her fault."],[123.04,"Everything was fine till she showed up."],[131.17,"Verse 13. So the Lord God said to the woman, What is this you have done?"],[138.29,"What is this you have done?"],[139.89,"Again, she can say, I disobeyed your commandment."],[142.77,"The woman said, The serpent deceived me and I hate"],[143.37,"Have mercy on me."],[144.25,"She could repent."],[149.37,"It's the serpent's fault."],[150.97,"It's his fault."],[153.75,"It's just a chain of blame."],[156.68,"This is how we know they're human."],[158.68,"Yes. Yes. And trying to justify themselves."],[168.68,"Verse 14. Thus the Lord God said to the serpent."],[172.76,"So you notice, he doesn't give the serpent a chance to repent."],[182.09,"He doesn't say to the serpent, What have you done?"],[185.13,"Why did you"],[187.73,"He's just gonna lay the proverbial smack down on the serpent."],[198.42,"Thus the Lord God said to the serpent, Because you have done this, you are cursed more than all cattle, and more than all the wild animals of the earth."],[207.7,"On your breast and belly you shall go, and you shall eat dust all the days of your life."],[213.06,"Okay, we'll pause there first."],[214.98,"Okay. So what's what's going on here?"],[221.3,"So, we already talked about who this is."],[224.04,"That this is this angelic being, who's now falling."],[227.74,"So, what was he trying to do?"],[228.38,"was he trying to What pull and why?"],[234.28,"Well, as we talked about, as we talked about, uh Milton's whole thing is right off the right, like this has nothing to do with trying to take over something."],[245.73,"Because he he can't do anything to God any more than you and I can."],[252.74,"He can do something to humans."],[255.54,"Why would he want to do something to humans?"],[262.74,"This is where Saint Andrew's envy comes in."],[268.02,"And this gets expressly in later Jewish literature. expressly spelled out"],[274.71,"This idea of him having this envy of human beings."],[282.17,"This envy of human beings."],[283.93,"Why would this highly exalted angelic being, or you get to Isaiah and Ezekiel in a couple of years, uh well?"],[292.97,"I'm back to doing that now."],[294.97,"Um go ahead."],[297.29,"It goes on and on about how glorious an angelic being he was."],[301.9,"Um, why would he be jealous of humans?"],[311.54,"And this has to do with salvation."],[315.66,"This is part of why it's important the point we made that humans were created innocent, not perfect."],[325.42,"Salvation is not about getting back to Eden."],[329.68,"Getting back to Eden is just starting over."],[334.64,"What were Adam and Eve created to do?"],[336.56,"We talked about the commandments they were given."],[340.4,"Fill the earth and subdue it."],[344.16,"And those two pieces were continuing the work of God in creation."],[348.72,"God put creation in order and then he filled it with life."],[352.5,"And the garden that he created, a garden is that sort of perfect combination where it's in order but also gives life."],[361.18,"It's not like a parking lot that's orderly but no life."],[364.14,"It's not like a swamp that's all life and no order."],[366.64,"But it's the perfect combination."],[368.88,"And so they were to turn the rest of the garden, the rest of the world into a garden."],[377.68,"They go forth and continue this creative work of God."],[381.12,"And by doing that, what would have happened to them?"],[385.68,"What we call theosis in the Orthodox Church."],[389.84,"By continuing to do the work of God, that would have transformed them."],[396.64,"And the state that they were destined to have ultimately in Christ, though the devil at this point didn't know how that was all going to work."],[402.88,"Paul told us"],[405.98,"We know because St."],[421.98,"Angelic beings don't get promoted."],[426.86,"It's not like, well, you've been doing a good job as an archangel."],[430.46,"I'm looking at your performance reviews."],[432.62,"We're going to try you out as a throne."],[435.66,"Maybe a dominion, you know."],[437.5,"Who knows how far you could go."],[439.83,"'s not that That's not how that works."],[445.28,"They don't get promoted."],[446.16,"promoted. In the incarnation we're celebrating right now, humanity gets"],[453.43,"In Christ, humanity gets lifted up and enthroned at the right hand of God."],[462.28,"That's the kind of thing that would make the devil jealous."],[468.76,"And if he's jealous of humanity about that, and he's angry at God about that, he can't do anything to God."],[478.28,"He could try and destroy humans and make sure they don't get there."],[484.4,"He could try and make humans like himself so that they won't become like God."],[488.32,"And so that's what he's trying to do"],[493.72,"He's trying to derail the whole thing."],[498.6,"And so this, I think it's called the curse."],[501.5,"That's put on that's put on him."],[505.02,"You're accursed more than all cattle and more than all the wild animals of the earth."],[510.14,"So when he was introduced, he was above all those creatures."],[516.94,"Now he's bel gonna be below all those creatures."],[522.62,"You were jealous of humans before, now you're gonna be jealous of dogs, cats, rats, insects."],[529.98,"You're gonna be down below and again this crawling crawling on your on your belly crawling on the the literally says in the Hebrew crawling the the the uh arets which can mean ground right or earth it's also a word that's used for the underworld um and notice it says you're gonna you're gonna eat dust all the days of your life now here's a place where we once again need to remember that eggship people are not stupid."],[567.06,"They did not think snakes, snakes ate dirt."],[570.9,"They had seen them eat mice and rats."],[574.66,"They have plenty of mice and rats in the ancient world."],[577.78,"They had seen snakes eat them."],[579.78,"They knew they didn't eat dust."],[581.14,"So what is this referring to?"],[582.92,"This isn't just referring to being a snake."],[587.8,"Where has the word dust, this word, afar, actually in Hebrew?"],[591.96,"That's that's that's translated dust."],[594.04,"Adam's made from it."],[595.56,"And in a few verses, Adam's gonna get told he's gonna return to it when he dies."],[604.0,"So this is an image of death."],[608.42,"This is an image of death."],[610.5,"Like Hebrews is going to talk about the devil as the one who holds the power of death."],[617.67,"Until Christ takes it away from him."],[619.87,"But until that point."],[621.37,"This is where he's getting the power of death."],[624.65,"This is why in a lot of iconography, you'll see Hades or the Abyss."],[632.43,"Represented, or Sheol."],[634.2,"Represented as this kind of gaping maw."],[638.38,"Like of this big serpent that's swallowing up the dead."],[642.3,"That's going back to this."],[646.62,"That's the devil."],[647.82,"That's what he's got."],[649.18,"He's got death and the dead until the harrowing of Hades, when Christ goes and takes that away from him, too."],[657.28,"But that's what he's got left."],[659.1,"And when we get, again, in a few years, when we get to Isaiah and Ezekiel that talk about this fall, they're going to use all of that imagery."],[661.9,"Of him making his bed on a pile of maggots"],[669.29,"The whole it gets grounded."],[670.65,"Yeah, the whole shebang."],[672.15,"Like all of the death imagery and decomposition and corruption."],[677.64,"That's a big fall."],[680.76,"From this glorious celestial intelligence to that."],[688.97,"So that's his, that's what he receives."],[691.85,"This is the place where the devil falls."],[694.89,"We're going to see some more angelic beings fall later as we go through the book of Genesis."],[701.21,"This actually happens spread out over a little bit of time."],[703.93,"But this is the devil"],[707.17,"And then verse 15, which I paused before because this is important to go into in some detail."],[716.69,"I will put enmity between you and the woman, and between your seed and her seed."],[724.05,"He shall bruise your head, and you shall be on guard for his heel."],[728.85,"That's an accurate translation of the Greek, but is lame."],[736.37,"So, what what the Hebrew is more like is uh he will crush your head and you will strike his heel."],[744.95,"That even like a s a serpent striking right his heel."],[748.55,"Notice how this is phrased"],[750.03,"But so there's enmity."],[755.71,"First of all, between you and the woman."],[760.83,"Not between you and humanity."],[764.83,"Not even between you and Adam."],[767.55,"Between you and the woman."],[772.19,"And then between your seed and her seed."],[780.59,"Why is that important?"],[781.71,"Well, we don't stop and think about this."],[783.87,"But especially as it was understood in the ancient world, women don't have seed."],[792.91,"The word in Greek is literally sperma."],[797.79,"Women don't have seed."],[799.95,"Men have seed."],[802.35,"So describing anyone as the seed of a woman is a weird construction."],[817.07,"And this is sort of mysterious and weird until we get to the virgin birth."],[826.67,"And this is why, for example, in our hymns in the Acathis that we do during Lent, conception without seed."],[837.47,"And why it's important that the word seed be there"],[839.19,"That's why that's important."],[844.19,"Conception without seed."],[845.55,"Christ is conceived, but there's no seed, meaning he's the seed of a woman."],[853.41,"To connect to this."],[854.93,"This is why, as we read here for Nativity, one of the epistle readings, St."],[862.13,"Paul's saying, born of a woman, born under the law."],[870.82,"He's making that connection back here."],[874.51,"So this isn't just telegraphing, oh, someday there's going to be a human descendant who's gonna resolve this issue by stomping, the the serpent, and something's gonna happen to him in the process."],[891.59,"But it's more specific than that."],[895.45,"And the way that woman is involved in this."],[898.65,"And this is why in we talked about this when we're going through St."],[903.45,"John's Gospel, but this is this is one of the things that he revisits, especially when you get close to the crucifixion of Christ, he starts pulling in all this Genesis language."],[913.09,"Um, and we've talked about how the Theotokos uh Virgin Mary goes from being called woman by Jesus through most of the Gospel of John to, well, he's on the cross being called Mother, the same way that Eve's name has been actually been Isha has been woman all the way through here."],[931.89,"She's gonna get the name Eve, Mother."],[937.33,"Yeah, and a few verses on after the expulsion from paradise."],[940.79,"That same connection."],[942.31,"But this is part of uh the connection to the Theotokos, and that connection runs through what we're gonna see in a few years, a couple years."],[954.11,"When we when we go through uh first and second Samuel and first and second kings, or first through fourth kingdoms, the kings of Judah, starting with Solomon, not the kings of the northern kingdom of Israel, only Judah, only David's line, when they're named, when they're coronated, says, This is his name, this is his mother."],[983.15,"The mothers of the Davidic kings are always listed."],[987.63,"And starting with Solomon and his mother Bathsheba of all people, uh they sat at the right hand of the king and were the top advisor."],[1000.43,"So this is the beginning of a tradition that starts here, runs through the whole Old Testament, and culminates in Christ and his mother."],[1019.19,"Verse 16. To the woman, he said, Okay, so that's we're done with the serpent."],[1024.79,"Now we've got consequences for the woman and man."],[1028.31,"And notice he goes in the reverse order of the way the blame got shifted."],[1033.59,"Now he's working his way back down the to the woman, he said, I will greatly multiply your pain and your groaning, and in pain you shall bring forth children."],[1043.51,"Your recourse will be to your husband, and he shall rule over you."],[1047.35,"That recourse is even makes it even more obscure than the original is."],[1051.75,"But yeah. So what's the first part?"],[1057.59,"Okay, so remember the two commandments God gave to man and woman."],[1066.59,"Fill the earth and subdue it."],[1069.67,"Put it in order, fill it with life."],[1074.31,"Those two commandments."],[1078.76,"One of the couple majors in, and the other one minors in."],[1083.98,"To use a collegiate metaphor."],[1087.1,"But they each are participating together because they're one flesh."],[1090.64,"But so remember, it's Adam who names the animals."],[1093.36,"And we talked about how that's part of the putting in order."],[1098.09,"He does that though with the participation and cooperation of woman."],[1104.54,"Filling the world with life, as we talked about, he couldn't do without her, literally."],[1111.74,"She obviously is crucial to filling the world with life, with human life."],[1118.96,"But obviously, he's participating in that."],[1122.9,"She's not doing that alone."],[1124.76,"He's participating in that."],[1126.04,"They're doing it together."],[1127.4,"So when the time comes here to the curse, to consequences."],[1134.09,"She's the one who's going to be most directly involved in bringing life into the world."],[1138.49,"That's going to be now painful, difficult, hard."],[1141.77,"Implying it would not have been before"],[1146.64,"But now that's going to be difficult, it's going to be hard."],[1148.88,"It's going to be a struggle."],[1149.92,"It's going to be painful."],[1151.04,"And this isn't just giving birth."],[1154.18,"There was a really dumb Victorian interpretation of this."],[1159.06,"Sorry, Arthur. I'm not actually a Victorian."],[1163.62,"No, but you're an apologist for them sometimes."],[1167.14,"I don't think they're hilarious."],[1169.94,"Um but uh where when when they first started finding ways to anesthetize women, shall we say, long before epidurals, but when they were first finding ways to help make ch.ildbirth less painful, there were people who opposed it"],[1190.54,"Based on a literal interpretation of this verse."],[1193.1,"They said, You're defying God by trying to make it less painful."],[1198.94,"Um kind of ridiculous."],[1202.28,"That's not what this is aimed at."],[1203.64,"Because this isn't just aimed at giving birth."],[1205.48,"It is talking about giving birth, but it's also talking about all the pain that comes with having children in a fallen and sinful world."],[1216.78,"The fear that comes with that."],[1219.11,"The dangers that come with that, the pain of losing a child."],[1224.01,"Because child mortality rates were insane in the ancient world."],[1228.93,"They had huge numbers of children, primarily because they would lose more than half of them before they reached adulthood."],[1235.89,"And usually the mother ended up dying in childbirth at some point down the line."],[1242.61,"All of that is involved here."],[1245.71,"In that pain and that suffering that's now going to be involved in filling the earth, with life."],[1254.85,"And this whole bit about the recourse or the desire being for your husband."],[1261.09,"Is this talking about the relationship between the two of them?"],[1265.83,"Which, as I just said, neither of them by themselves separately could fulfill the commandments that God had given them together."],[1276.28,"They need each other, they need to work together."],[1278.76,"And this is saying that is going to be difficult."],[1284.3,"He's saying to the woman, you're gonna want to take charge."],[1288.3,"And he's going to."],[1289.48,"And it's going to become this sort of struggle for dominance and power between the two of you instead of cooperation."],[1302.25,"Now notice, none of these things are God doing something to them."],[1311.05,"It's not God saying, I'm going to torture you while you're giving birth."],[1314.41,"It's saying this is this is the consequence now"],[1319.86,"Now you know about evil."],[1323.38,"That's what this means."],[1325.71,"That's what this means to your relationship now that both of you know evil."],[1330.45,"God's not going to go in there and stir up trouble in their marriage."],[1333.19,"But like this is going to happen."],[1335.03,"It's going to come from you."],[1338.95,"Verse 17, then to Adam he said, Because you heeded the voice of your wife and ate from the one tree of which I commanded you, saying, You shall not eat from it."],[1351.83,"Cursed is the ground in your labors."],[1354.23,"In toil you shall eat from it all the days of your life."],[1356.71,"of Both thorns and thistles it shall bring forth for you, and you shall eat the herb the field, in the sweat of your face you shall eat bread, till you return to the ground from which you were taken."],[1370.59,"Earth you are, and to earth you shall return."],[1381.31,"Two pieces here."],[1383.04,"Notice first that he says, Because you obeyed the woman, meaning you didn't obey God."],[1394.16,"You chose instead to obey her."],[1396.98,"Why is that important?"],[1398.26,"Well, because remember what his excuse was."],[1400.78,"Oh, it wasn't me, it was her."],[1403.83,"And he's affirming to Adam, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no."],[1407.03,"She didn't do this to you."],[1409.67,"You decided to."],[1411.96,"Follow her. Because of that."],[1416.14,"Now, notice it's it's cursed is the ground because of you."],[1421.26,"This that I'm emphasizing that wording because next week when we talk about chapter four, that wording is going to become important."],[1429.34,"But cursed is the ground because of you, and what does that mean?"],[1432.72,"That means, trying to try to turn the world into a garden."],[1437.02,"Now you're part of that."],[1439.19,"Putting it in order to bring forth food, that's gonna be difficult."],[1441.99,"That's gonna be a struggle"],[1442.83,"That's gonna be painful."],[1445.63,"You're gonna struggle to get enough food to eat out of the ground."],[1450.21,"Just to keep yourself alive."],[1452.9,"And notice this shift."],[1455.06,"We've mentioned this before, but there's the shift from it was eating the fruit from trees."],[1461.22,"Nothing dies. You're not killing anything."],[1464.18,"And that represented creation sort of offering itself to humanity to nourish and feed humanity."],[1471.83,"Creation now has a different relationship to humanity."],[1478.25,"It's not gonna offer itself up."],[1480.81,"It's barely gonna cooperate."],[1482.65,"You're not going to just be able to pick it off the trees"],[1486.93,"You're going to have to work the ground and struggle and grow it."],[1492.05,"And then eat it."],[1494.05,"And so your part of this is going to be difficult now."],[1497.41,"It's going to be a struggle."],[1498.37,"It's going to be painful."],[1501.81,"And you're going to have to do it every day of your life."],[1506.77,"You're going to have to work just to stay alive."],[1510.29,"And ultimately. Ashes to ashes, dust to dust."],[1515.42,"You're going to return to the ground from which you were taken."],[1519.68,"You're going to physically die."],[1527.2,"Verse 20. So Adam called his wife's name life because she was the mother of all living"],[1532.84,"That's a the the reason for that, the reason they did that in the Orthodox Study Bible, is that uh the Greek actually translates the name Eve."],[1544.04,"It doesn't transliterate Eve like a name."],[1547.82,"Eva means uh mother."],[1551.92,"Because she says uh the mother of all living."],[1554.4,"Um they translated it as Zoe in the Greek, which means life."],[1561.6,"And so they wanted to point that out."],[1564.56,"So they did that in the butt but so this is part of this change."],[1569.5,"Yes, sir. Is there why do you think that Adam doesn't name her?"],[1575.46,"Because I mean, like, you could have named her right when we called her woman, but I will call you woman because you came from man."],[1582.98,"Is this the same kind of name you did with the animals?"],[1586.26,"Or is it significant or something?"],[1588.82,"I I think it's either that her name is changed."],[1591.06,"The idea is that it's now changed."],[1594.59,"That she's now the mother, the mother of all living."],[1597.95,"I think that's the same thing that St."],[1599.71,"John sees going on when he makes that change from woman to to mother."],[1604.89,"With the Theotogos."],[1606.01,"So now it's a change of role."],[1609.98,"Um that's a more positive one."],[1612.14,"This is a negative one."],[1614.38,"Is that change? in rule because that relationship is now strained"],[1619.06,"Since your relationships are gonna be button heads and five."],[1623.86,"Yeah. It's inappropriate to say you're they don't sound similar anymore."],[1629.14,"Yeah. Yeah, yeah."],[1630.98,"Because remember he said, I'll call call you woman because you came from man."],[1635.88,"And you are bone of my bone and flesh of my flesh."],[1643.1,"And that relationship now is very different."],[1645.34,"Yeah, she's yeah."],[1647.98,"Like you want a rule is already happening."],[1651.34,"Yeah. Yeah. Yeah."],[1660.42,"So verse 21."],[1661.78,"Also, for Adam and his wife, the Lord God made garments of skin and clothed them."],[1669.62,"Um, uh what's going on here?"],[1677.46,"So a lot of folks again want to take this literally."],[1681.3,"Like, oh, you did a lousy job with those fig leaves."],[1684.02,"Let me give you some leather clothes."],[1686.34,"They'll they'll last longer and do a little better out there in the in the wild world."],[1690.87,"Um, that's not what's going on here."],[1693.4,"So, why is it garments of skins?"],[1696.52,"Well, what happens here?"],[1698.12,"God's killing something."],[1701.9,"So some animals get. killed"],[1706.34,"Why would God kill some animals?"],[1709.46,"So they know what death is."],[1713.84,"What does that mean?"],[1716.0,"Here's what it means."],[1719.09,"Number one. And number two, the garments of skin that are here being talked about is this is gonna sound crazy for a second, but bear with me."],[1729.81,"It's referring to a change in their bodies."],[1735.33,"Change in their bodies."],[1737.17,"This is going back to something we talked about way back in the long ago time when we were in St."],[1741.65,"Paul. I think when we were in 1 Corinthians, we talked about this at some length."],[1746.65,"And that's when we hear the word body, as modern people, we think meat."],[1754.58,"We think physical stuff."],[1756.44,"That's your body."],[1759.24,"That is not how ancient people, including the writers of the Old and New Testaments, thought about it."],[1767.08,"Because they distinguish, for example, between in Greek soma and sarx."],[1773.58,"Body and flesh."],[1776.06,"Those two things are talked about in different ways."],[1779.36,"So meat. This is flesh."],[1783.66,"Body, what a body meant was a sort of of nexus powers or abilities or potentialities."],[1793.78,"Capacities. Sort of the way that's later when we get to Greek terminology in theology, what we're going to call nature is very similar to the way that Hebrew writers use the term body."],[1810.6,"So St. Paul, the reason this is why we talked about it in 1 Corinthians, in 1 Corinthians 15, he talks about different kinds of bodies."],[1819.98,"He says the sun, moon, and stars have one kind of body, and the animals have another kind of body, and humans have another kind of body."],[1828.96,"And you're kind of going, stars?"],[1831.97,"It seems pretty clear there because he refers to them as celestials, and he's talking about kind of angels."],[1836.61,"You're kind of going, well, wait a minute."],[1838.05,"I thought angels didn't have bodies."],[1841.65,"Well, they don't have meat."],[1844.58,"But from that ancient perspective of body, they do."],[1847.46,"This is why I say John of Damascus is going to say angels are bodiless compared to us."],[1853.27,"But they have bodies in the sense that as a finite creature."],[1858.97,"An angel is a finite creature."],[1860.57,"Any finite creature has a finite set of powers and abilities, of things they can do."],[1866.86,"And be, and you like nature."],[1870.3,"Um, we still get. and we've been hearing this a lot, because we just celebrated nativity"],[1875.3,"Who knows when this recording will go up?"],[1877.38,"So maybe well into Lent."],[1879.62,"Um, but um just celebrate nativity."],[1883.78,"A lot of the hymns still use that older understanding of body because they'll talk about Christ taking a body, and that doesn't just mean like God took a human physical body, it's using body in that broad sense to talk about human nature or humanity as a whole."],[1904.3,"And this is this is part of why we have trouble understanding what the the church fathers say about how the incarnation works."],[1915.27,"But if we understand body in that sense, and we understand human nature in that sense, what it means for Christ to take on our human nature is that he adds to himself the range of human powers and potentialities."],[1931.61,"That are not proper to God."],[1934.49,"God doesn't sleep."],[1937.26,"Humans can sleep."],[1947.19,"And we could talk about Christ doing things qua God or qua human."],[1952.4,"But the idea is that he adds."],[1955.46,"It's additive. So he doesn't stop being God and turn into a human."],[1962.28,"He doesn't lose his omniscience, omnipotence, whatever, whatever, however we want to categorize those."],[1968.68,"He adds our human powers and potentialities."],[1974.73,"So what's happening here, when they're given garments of skin."],[1980.99,"They're being given what will later be called in theological terms, mortal flesh."],[1986.71,"A body which is suited to certain things."],[1989.83,"And St. John of Damascus points out one thing in particular it's suited to, that's repentance."],[1997.59,"So he connects our mortality. the fact that our bodies become corrupt"],[2008.03,"They're generated. We grow to maturity, and then it falls off."],[2013.25,"Over the hill like me."],[2018.13,"And things start to break down."],[2020.13,"That mutability, that ability to change and be changed."],[2025.67,"That an angel doesn't have because it's immortal and unchanging."],[2032.97,"But that we have, that allows us to repent."],[2038.83,"It makes us mortal."],[2039.95,"It means we're subject to death, but it also means we can repent and turn back to God."],[2044.71,"Is that we're coming under time in that."],[2050.87,"Well, at least that however time was experienced before the in paradise is different than how we experience it."],[2059.51,"Yeah. Yeah. Whether time actually exists as a thing is a whole other question."],[2064.47,"And a rabbit hole we don't need to go down."],[2066.79,"But the way time would have been experienced."],[2070.96,"Is is very different."],[2072.08,"And and the f the the church fathers very early on say this."],[2076.34,"They say that there it's not like there was a bunch of time that passed between when the angels were created and fell or when humans were created and fell."],[2085.22,"We don't see any time lapse in here in the garden."],[2087.74,"Like, was it an hour, a day, a week, a month?"],[2093.12,"There's no time lapse because the whole experience of time would have been a different thing."],[2099.86,"Then we can't understand that because we're humans who experience it in a certain way."],[2105.16,"Yeah. Um. But so, and and this is going back again to 1 Corinthians 15 and how St."],[2112.45,"Paul understands this."],[2113.89,"This is why he talks about in the resurrection, our mortality being clothed with immortality."],[2121.25,"He uses this garment language again."],[2126.31,"This uses his garment language again to describe the switch in the other direction."],[2129.67,"So here they're being clothed with mortality"],[2134.75,"They're being clothed with death."],[2140.91,"And on the other side in the resurrection, we'll be clothed with immortality."],[2146.91,"Which is not just reversing this."],[2150.56,"But is taking this to its point of completion."],[2154.85,"In Christ. And now some more about death."],[2160.37,"Verse 22 Then the Lord God said, Behold, the man is become like one of us to know good and evil."],[2170.05,"Now, lest he put out his hand and take also of the tree of life. and eat and live forever"],[2175.93,"Therefore the Lord God sent him out of the garden of pleasure to cultivate the ground from which he was taken."],[2185.69,"So why are humans expelled from paradise?"],[2196.57,"Because God says it would not be good, we've got this good not good."],[2201.9,"It would not be good for humanity in this present state to go and eat from the tree of life and become immortal."],[2213.46,"Because what is immortal and knows good and evil?"],[2217.94,"Well, the devil for one."],[2223.43,"So humanity would become like the demons."],[2226.15,"And what would that mean?"],[2228.87,"That would mean the devil had succeeded in his little plot here."],[2238.2,"And so this mortality being given for repentance."],[2243.26,"Being cast out of paradise, so that we will be mortal."],[2249.63,"Is God showing mercy on us and giving us this life in this world as an opportunity to repent and return to Him."],[2264.07,"The idea being that at least potentially, someone who refuses to do that could end up where they would have been originally."],[2275.95,"But this window is given."],[2278.05,"This opportunity is given to us for repentance."],[2284.53,"And that's why a mortal life in this world ending in death is given to us as this gift."],[2291.89,"So this is the opposite of death being the death penalty."],[2299.33,"This is the opposite of God punishing. us today because Adam disobeyed a commandment however long ago"],[2309.05,"We're not going opening that can of worms, but however long ago."],[2314.94,"He didn't say the day you eat of it, I will kill you."],[2320.91,"He said, you will die."],[2325.47,"Now, since I just referenced that, maybe wondering, well, wait a minute."],[2330.67,"We just read about the day he ate from it, and he didn't die."],[2335.76,"So St. John of Damascus, when he references this, says there's two kinds of death."],[2344.48,"There's physical death. in which the soul, the life, is separated from the body"],[2351.32,"And there's spiritual death in which the soul is separated from God."],[2357.48,"The soul, the life, our life is separated from God."],[2362.44,"And the way we as modern people think about it, modern people who are religious, is that, well, physical death is real death."],[2373.33,"And then this spiritual death thing is like an analogy."],[2377.91,"Or sort of an allegory."],[2379.69,"A way of talking about sin or something."],[2383.93,"But the way Genesis presents it, and what St."],[2388.41,"John of Damascus points out. is that it's actually exactly the opposite"],[2393.97,"Real death is our life being cut off from God."],[2398.85,"That's what death is."],[2402.77,"Physical death is analogous to it."],[2408.53,"And is actually a result of it."],[2415.89,"In St. John's gospel, Christ says, this is life to know you, the only true God, and Jesus Christ, whom you've sent."],[2428.37,"That's what life is."],[2429.73,"Not biological life."],[2433.45,"Knowing God. Biological life is sort of an image of it"],[2434.67,"That's real life."],[2441.07,"So what St."],[2442.99,"John understands is happening here is that as soon as Adam disobeys, as soon as evil comes into the picture, he experiences spiritual death."],[2457.15,"It's like if you took and tied a tourniquet around one of your fingers today and left it on."],[2466.67,"Eventually, it's gonna die."],[2469.23,"Tissue's gonna necrotize."],[2470.99,"Gangrene's going to set in"],[2473.07,"Eventually, it's just gonna fall off."],[2476.44,"And that's what happens here."],[2479.68,"When Adam and Eve die spiritually and they're cut off from God, it's like tying a tourniquet."],[2486.56,"And because of that, eventually they're going to physically die."],[2491.92,"Their body's going to die and return to dust."],[2495.89,"So there's going to be hope."],[2498.29,"But that's what's being set up here is that physical death is a consequence of spiritual death."],[2504.21,"And is the real death."],[2508.13,"Verse 24. So he cast out Adam and made him to dwell opposite the garden of pleasure."],[2513.17,"He then stationed the cherubim in the fiery sword, which turns every way to guard the way to the tree of life."],[2521.37,"Cherubim do what?"],[2523.61,"They protect the place where God is."],[2530.17,"Not because Adam is a threat to God, but because God's holy presence now is a threat to Adam."],[2537.85,"He needs to be kept away from the tree of life, at least for now."],[2543.77,"We just did Revelation before we looped around."],[2546.01,"So we saw the tree of life show up again and everyone eating from it."],[2550.47,"In uh at the end of the book of Revelation."],[2552.71,"But for now."],[2554.93,"Because man is mankind is silly."],[2557.33,"He has to be he has to be kept away from it."],[2560.45,"So we're ending on a huge downer."],[2565.73,"'s. Oh, yeah, it not gonna, it's gonna get worse before it gets better here in the book of Genesis"],[2574.57,"But but important takeaways here in terms of how we talk about this."],[2580.7,"Um as we go through, we've we've now completed the first quote-unquote fall of humanity."],[2588.86,"There's gonna be two more before we're done with the first 11 chapters of Genesis."],[2600.7,"The word sin has not appeared yet in the Bible."],[2606.06,"So we're not really dealing talking about sin yet."],[2608.7,"We've seen the devil, we haven't really seen demons yet."],[2610.62,"This is talking about death"],[2614.31,"This is how death happens."],[2620.31,"There's gonna be these three."],[2622.15,"And in early Christianity, in the church fathers, you find them talking about all three of these."],[2630.47,"Any given individual church father is gonna emphasize usually one of them over the other two."],[2637.43,"Without like disavowing the other two, but just they're gonna focus on one of them."],[2642.95,"So, for example, Saint Irenaeus is gonna focus on basically Genesis 4 through 9."],[2650.79,"Starting with Cain leading up to the flood."],[2653.68,"That's that's St."],[2654.24,"'s That's where he going to focus."],[2655.4,"Irenaeus in the second century."],[2659.56,"Eusebius of Caesarea, if you read his um, what is it?"],[2665.08,"It's the uh something of the gospel."],[2670.2,"Um discourse of the gospel, presentation of the gospel, something like that."],[2674.52,"It's not coming to me right now."],[2676.28,"Um he is gonna emphasize what happens in Genesis 10 and 11, the Tower of Babel, and the dividing of the nations."],[2688.52,"That's what he's gonna emphasize."],[2690.28,"And very famously, St."],[2691.56,"Augustine is gonna emphasize what we just read."],[2694.9,"As being the key thing."],[2697.14,"That's all well and good."],[2698.28,"St. Augustine's in good company, he's like any other church father."],[2698.76,"He emphasizes one of them"],[2702.16,"Problem is, Saint Augustine, out of those people I just named, is the only one who writes in Latin."],[2710.72,"And even at the time St."],[2712.16,"Augustine lived, he couldn't really read anything but Latin."],[2718.0,"Going forward, nobody in the West could really read anything but Latin."],[2722.16,"And so Western theology becomes based almost entirely on St."],[2727.44,"Augustine. And because of that, we as people who have grown up and lived in the West, regardless of our background, we've gotten this emphasis on the fall."],[2741.12,"This is where everything goes wrong for humanity."],[2743.88,"This is this is just some of the stuff that goes wrong."],[2747.56,"And this has become very freighted."],[2750.78,"Beyond just death and the things that we talked about."],[2754.94,"And due to his own St."],[2758.78,"Augustine's own views of justice and things, the idea of death as a death penalty."],[2763.36,"All those things have gotten sort of inherited in the West."],[2765.92,"So part of I just want to make clear by going through Genesis 1 through 3 the way I did over the last three Bible studies, uh, I am deliberately saying we need to set aside that other stuff."],[2781.92,"That's right, that it's not helpful."],[2786.8,"As we go forward into Genesis 4, we're going to start talking about sin."],[2790.76,"And we're going to have a different understanding of sin, too."],[2795.49,"Because as I pointed out when we finish chapter 3, the word sin has not appeared yet."],[2801.41,"So at the very least, we shouldn't be taking Adam's breaking of a commandment as the emblematic instance of sin, because it's not even called that in the text."],[2813.89,"But sin's going to pop up pretty quick in chapter 4."],[2817.97,"And so that's where we should, because that's where, and as we'll talk about next time, that's where the New Testament goes when it wants to talk about archetypal sin."],[2831.25,"That's where we focus."],[2832.21,"So we don't need to freight everything down, into one of these, even though I know we've inherited a lot of that, in our thinking."],[2844.11,"This is a story of how humanity in our youth, from the beginning rebelled against God, and how the world that's full of sin and death that we live in now is the consequence of that."],[2861.04,"But it is not a story of God being angry at us, quite the opposite."],[2866.17,"At every point, God is merciful toward humanity."],[2869.45,"He's not really merciful toward the serpent, but he's merciful toward humanity."],[2873.87,"All through this."],[2877.48,"And so this this is the understanding it's aimed at."],[2881.0,"We're going to get into sin and maliciousness and evil that we perpetrate on each other."],[2886.84,"That we're going there next, but that's not what the expulsion from paradise is about."],[2895.13,"It's a very different thing."],[2896.57,"Yes, sir. This is just putting back things that you've said in the past."],[2902.01,"That we don't have the idea that Adam's sin is inherited by Adam."],[2908.35,"There's nothing you're doing for us."],[2909.6,"You are not guilty of what Adam did."],[2912.16,"Yeah, we're only guilty of our own self, which is enough."],[2915.42,"Uh there's nothing even in this text to say that Adam is guilty of what Adam did."],[2924.18,"In the sense if we be guilt as liable to some kind of punishment."],[2931.4,"Like there's no He doesn't get punished because death is not a penalty."],[2937.32,"Death is given as a mercy so that humanity won't be immortal and evil."],[2944.7,"I mean that that is uh there's actually a miniseries many years ago that nobody watched about this where they had a world where no one could die anymore."],[2957.66,"Death disappeared. And so if you got cancer, that was forever."],[2966.67,"When you were enfeebled at old age, that was forever."],[2971.72,"Pain forever. Injury forever."],[2974.6,"It's a nightmare."],[2976.62,"It's hell on earth."],[2980.27,"With that taken away."],[2982.51,"Which is not how we think about it."],[2984.77,"But is the reality."],[2986.05,"And it's the reality that's being pointed to here."],[2990.21,"Um part of part of that, I think."],[2994.93,"Um I don't want to go too much longer, but part part of that I think has come from the modern life we live right I don't think you have to go back that far in history the average poor person in like the 18th or 19th century if you ask them would you like to live forever like this would not say yes that's they would not right we may think oh I want to live forever like this that's because our lives must be going okay right that's right and and uh when when someone passes away, when someone passes away young or even at old age now."],[3042.79,"All we think about is oh, all the things they missed out on."],[3044.75,"things All these good things and happy that we enjoy."],[3044.99,"they Like didn't think that way in like the 17th, 18th, 19th century."],[3055.01,"In a lot of cases, they thought about all the hardships and difficulties they missed, they were spared."],[3061.27,"And so that's I think part of why we're out of out of touch with this."],[3067.35,"And um thanks from people who are into technological optimisms saying that we are uh on the verge of of abolishing death, or we if we can now think forward that we will succeed in abolishing death, I thought no, yeah."],[3084.71,"Don't do that."],[3085.35,"Well, and also good luck, but yeah yeah okay so we've gone really long tonight but this is it obviously this is a kind of important chapter of the Bible so thank you everybody listen next time as Father Stephen DeYoung continues his study of the scriptures on the Whole Counsel of God father Stephen's email address is wholecounsel at ancient faith dot com that's wholecounsel at ancient faith dot com"]],"o":[{"t":21.44,"lv":2,"h":"3:9-11 - \"Adam, where are you?\"","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>3:9</b>: Lord God called Adam: \"<b>where are you?</b>\" - not because he doesn't know, but <b>because he does</b></li><li class=\"d0\">(finishing 3:8) \"voice of the Lord walking\" comes from that word</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>3:10</b>: \"I heard your voice... I was afraid because I was naked, so I hid\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"not a good excuse\" if covering up - bunch of immediate questions</li><li class=\"d1\">why afraid? how'd you know you were naked? what made you think you could <b>hide from God behind a tree</b>?</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>3:11</b>: \"Who said you were naked? Have you eaten from the one tree...?\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Opportunities to <b>confess, repent, seek forgiveness</b> - like in church: \"Yes, I did. I was wrong. Have mercy on me\"</li></ul>"},{"t":106.25,"lv":2,"h":"3:12-13 - The chain of blame","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>3:12</b>: Adam: \"the woman <b>you gave me</b> gave me of the tree and I ate\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"wasn't me\" - really <b>God's fault</b> for putting her there; if not, hers; \"everything was fine till she showed up\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>3:13</b>: God to woman: \"<b>What is this you have done?</b>\" - she could say \"I disobeyed\", repent</li><li class=\"d1\">instead: \"<b>the serpent deceived me</b>\" - \"it's his fault\"</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Just a chain of blame\" - \"this is how we know they're human\"; trying to <b>justify themselves</b></li></ul>"},{"t":168.68,"lv":2,"h":"3:14 - The curse on the serpent","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>3:14</b>: God to serpent - <b>no chance to repent</b></li><li class=\"d1\">doesn't ask \"what have you done?\" - \"lay the proverbial smack down\"</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Cursed more than all cattle and all wild animals; on your <b>breast and belly</b> you shall go, <b>eat dust</b> all the days of your life\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Pause: what's going on?</li></ul>"},{"t":214.98,"lv":3,"h":"Why the devil did it: envy","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">The angelic being now <b>falling</b> - what was he trying to do?</li><li class=\"d0\">Milton's \"take over\" idea is out - can't do anything to <b>God</b> any more than you and I can</li><li class=\"d1\">he <b>can</b> do something to humans - why?</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>St. Andrew's envy</b> - spelled out expressly in later <b>Jewish literature</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>envy of human beings</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Isaiah and Ezekiel (in a couple of years) go on about how <b>glorious</b> an angelic being he was</li><li class=\"d0\">Why jealous of humans? → has to do with <b>salvation</b></li></ul>"},{"t":311.54,"lv":3,"h":"Humans created innocent, not perfect; theosis","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Key point: created <b>innocent, not perfect</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Salvation is <b>not getting back to Eden</b> - that's \"just starting over\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Adam and Eve's commandments: <b>fill the earth and subdue it</b> = continuing God's work</li><li class=\"d1\">God <b>put creation in order</b>, then <b>filled it with life</b></li><li class=\"d1\">garden = perfect combination: order + life - \"not a parking lot (orderly, no life), not a swamp (life, no order)\"</li><li class=\"d1\">they were to turn the rest of the world into a garden</li><li class=\"d0\">By doing God's work → <b>theosis</b> - transformed</li><li class=\"d1\">destined state ultimately <b>in Christ</b> - though devil didn't know how it would work</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Angelic beings don't get promoted</b> - no performance reviews, \"try you out as a throne, maybe a dominion\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Incarnation</b> (celebrating now): humanity <b>lifted up, enthroned at right hand of God</b> → \"would make the devil jealous\"</li><li class=\"d0\">He can't touch God → destroy humans, or <b>make them like himself</b> so they won't become like God; \"derail the whole thing\"</li></ul>"},{"t":498.6,"lv":3,"h":"The curse: below all creatures","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Introduced <b>above</b> all creatures; now <b>below</b> them</li><li class=\"d1\">\"jealous of dogs, cats, rats, insects\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Crawling on belly - Hebrew <i>arets</i> = ground/earth, also word for the <b>underworld</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"Eat dust\" - Egyptians not stupid: they'd seen snakes eat mice and rats, <b>not dust</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Not just about being a snake</li></ul>"},{"t":581.14,"lv":2,"h":"Dust = death; the serpent and Hades","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><i>Afar</i> = dust: <b>Adam made from it</b>; in a few verses told he'll <b>return to it</b></li><li class=\"d0\">→ image of <b>death</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Hebrews</b>: devil holds the <b>power of death</b> until Christ takes it away</li><li class=\"d0\">Iconography: <b>Hades / Abyss / Sheol</b> as <b>gaping maw of a big serpent swallowing the dead</b></li><li class=\"d1\">he keeps death and the dead until the <b>harrowing of Hades</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Isaiah, Ezekiel</b> (later) use that imagery: <b>bed on a pile of maggots</b>, death, decomposition, corruption</li><li class=\"d0\">\"A big fall\" from glorious celestial intelligence</li><li class=\"d0\">Place where the devil falls; <b>more angels fall later</b> in Genesis - spread over time</li></ul>"},{"t":707.17,"lv":2,"h":"3:15 - Enmity and the seed","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>3:15</b>: enmity between you and the woman, your seed and her seed; \"he shall bruise your head, you shall be on guard for his heel\"</li><li class=\"d1\">accurate Greek, but \"lame\"; Hebrew: he will <b>crush your head</b>, you will <b>strike his heel</b> - a serpent striking</li><li class=\"d0\">Enmity between serpent and <b>the woman</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not humanity, not even Adam</li><li class=\"d0\">Then <b>your seed and her seed</b></li></ul>"},{"t":780.59,"lv":2,"h":"Seed of the woman: the virgin birth","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Why important: in the ancient world <b>women don't have seed</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Greek <i>sperma</i>; men have seed → \"seed of a woman\" = weird construction</li><li class=\"d0\">Mysterious until the <b>virgin birth</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Akathist</b> hymns in Lent: \"<b>conception without seed</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">Christ conceived with no seed = <b>seed of a woman</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Nativity</b> epistle: Paul, \"<b>born of a woman</b>, born under the law\" - connecting back here</li><li class=\"d0\">Not just \"some human descendant will someday stomp the serpent\" - more specific, and woman is involved</li></ul>"},{"t":898.65,"lv":3,"h":"Woman to Mother: Theotokos and the queen mothers","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>John's Gospel</b>: near the crucifixion pulls in Genesis language</li><li class=\"d1\">Mary called <b>woman</b> by Jesus through most of John → on the cross <b>mother</b></li><li class=\"d1\">same as Eve: <i>Isha</i> = woman throughout → named <b>Eve, mother</b> a few verses after expulsion</li><li class=\"d0\">Connection to the <b>Theotokos</b> runs through <b>Samuel / Kings</b> (kingdoms)</li><li class=\"d1\">only <b>Judah, David's line</b>: coronation notes \"this is his name, this is his <b>mother</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">mothers of Davidic kings always listed</li><li class=\"d1\">from <b>Solomon and Bathsheba</b>: sat at the <b>right hand of the king</b>, top advisor</li><li class=\"d0\">Tradition starts here → whole OT → culminates in <b>Christ and his mother</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1019.19,"lv":2,"h":"3:16 - Consequences for the woman","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Done with serpent; now woman and man - in <b>reverse order of the blame shifting</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>3:16</b>: \"greatly multiply your pain and groaning; in pain you shall bring forth children; your recourse to your husband, he shall rule over you\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"recourse\" even more obscure than the original</li></ul>"},{"t":1051.75,"lv":3,"h":"Childbirth, and the struggle between them","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Two commandments: <b>fill the earth, subdue it</b> - put in order, fill with life</li><li class=\"d1\">one \"majors in\" each, other \"minors\" - but together, <b>one flesh</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Adam names the animals</b> (order) with the woman's cooperation; filling with life - he couldn't without her, but he participates</li><li class=\"d0\">Curse hits where <b>she's most directly involved</b>: bringing life → now <b>painful, difficult</b> (implies it wasn't before)</li><li class=\"d0\">Not just giving birth: dumb <b>Victorian</b> interpretation - opposed anesthetizing childbirth as defying God</li><li class=\"d1\">aim is <b>all the pain of having children in a fallen world</b>: fear, dangers, <b>losing a child</b></li><li class=\"d1\">ancient child mortality; mothers often died in childbirth</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>\"Desire for your husband\"</b> = the relationship between them</li><li class=\"d1\">neither could fulfill commandments alone - need to <b>work together</b> - now difficult</li><li class=\"d1\">you'll want to take charge → <b>struggle for dominance</b> instead of cooperation</li><li class=\"d0\">None of this is <b>God doing something to them</b> - not \"I'll torture you\"; <b>consequence</b> now that both know evil</li><li class=\"d1\">God won't stir up trouble in the marriage - it comes <b>from you</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1338.95,"lv":2,"h":"3:17-19 - Consequences for Adam","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>3:17-19</b>: because you heeded your wife's voice... <b>cursed is the ground</b>; toil; <b>thorns and thistles</b>; sweat of your face; \"<b>earth you are, to earth you shall return</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Because you obeyed the woman\" = you didn't obey God</li><li class=\"d1\">answers his excuse: she didn't do it to you; <b>you decided</b> to follow her</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Cursed is the ground <b>because of you</b>\" - wording to be important in <b>chapter 4</b> next week</li><li class=\"d0\">Meaning: turning the world into a garden - now hard to get food from the ground, \"just to keep yourself alive\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Shift: fruit from trees - nothing dies - creation <b>offering itself</b> to nourish humanity</li><li class=\"d1\">now creation \"barely gonna cooperate\"; <b>work the ground</b>, grow it, then eat</li><li class=\"d1\">every day of your life</li><li class=\"d0\">Ultimately \"ashes to ashes\": <b>you will physically die</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1527.2,"lv":2,"h":"3:20 - Eve: mother of all living","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>3:20</b>: Adam called wife's name <b>life</b>, mother of all living</li><li class=\"d1\">Orthodox Study Bible follows Greek: translates <i>Eve</i> as <i>Zoe</i> = life, not transliterated</li><li class=\"d0\">Part of this change</li><li class=\"d0\">Q: why doesn't Adam name her earlier? (just \"woman\" because from man)</li><li class=\"d1\">her name <b>changed</b> - now <b>mother of all living</b>; same thing <b>John</b> sees: woman → mother with the Theotokos</li><li class=\"d1\">change of <b>role</b>: that one more positive, this one negative</li><li class=\"d1\">\"woman\" = \"bone of my bone, flesh of my flesh\" - relationship now very different; rule already happening</li></ul>"},{"t":1660.42,"lv":2,"h":"3:21 - Garments of skin","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>3:21</b>: Lord God made <b>garments of skin</b> and clothed them</li><li class=\"d0\">Folks take literally: \"lousy fig leaves, here's leather\" - <b>not what's going on</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Why skins? God <b>kills something</b></li><li class=\"d1\">so they <b>know what death is</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Number two: \"sounds crazy, bear with me\" - refers to <b>a change in their bodies</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1719.09,"lv":3,"h":"\"Body\" means capacities, not meat","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">From <b>1 Corinthians</b>: moderns hear body = <b>meat, physical stuff</b>; not how OT/NT writers thought</li><li class=\"d0\">Greek <i>soma</i> (body) vs <i>sarx</i> (flesh)</li><li class=\"d0\">Body = <b>nexus of powers, abilities, potentialities, capacities</b></li><li class=\"d1\">close to what theology later calls <b>nature</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>1 Cor 15</b>: sun, moon, stars one kind of body; animals another; humans another</li><li class=\"d1\">stars = <b>celestials</b> = angels; \"angels didn't have bodies?\" - no <b>meat</b>, but body in the ancient sense</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>John of Damascus</b>: angels bodiless <b>compared to us</b>; finite creature → <b>finite set of powers</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Nativity hymns: Christ \"taking a body\" = human nature / humanity as a whole</li></ul>"},{"t":1904.3,"lv":3,"h":"Incarnation is additive","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Why we struggle with fathers on incarnation - if \"body\" = nature</li><li class=\"d0\">Christ takes our nature → <b>adds</b> human powers and potentialities not proper to God</li><li class=\"d1\">God doesn't sleep; humans can</li><li class=\"d1\">talk of Christ <i>qua</i> God / <i>qua</i> human</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Additive</b>: doesn't stop being God, doesn't lose omniscience, omnipotence</li></ul>"},{"t":1974.73,"lv":3,"h":"Garments of skin = mortal flesh, for repentance","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Given what's later called <b>mortal flesh</b> - a body suited to certain things</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>John of Damascus</b>: suited to <b>repentance</b></li><li class=\"d1\">bodies corrupt: generated, grow to maturity, then break down - \"over the hill like me\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>mutability</b> - an angel doesn't have it (immortal, unchanging)</li><li class=\"d1\">makes us mortal, subject to death - but lets us <b>repent and turn back</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Coming <b>under time</b>? - time in paradise experienced differently; \"rabbit hole\"</li><li class=\"d1\">fathers: no time lapse between angels' creation and fall, or humans' - hour? week? <b>no lapse in the text</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>1 Cor 15</b>: <b>mortality clothed with immortality</b> - garment language again</li><li class=\"d1\">here: clothed with <b>mortality, death</b>; resurrection: clothed with <b>immortality</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not reversing this but <b>taking it to completion in Christ</b></li></ul>"},{"t":2154.85,"lv":2,"h":"3:22-23 - Expelled from paradise","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>3:22-23</b>: man become like one of us, knowing good and evil; <b>lest he take of the tree of life and live forever</b> → sent out to cultivate the ground</li><li class=\"d0\">Why expelled: <b>not good</b> to eat of tree of life in this state and become immortal</li><li class=\"d1\">what's immortal and knows good and evil? <b>the devil</b>, for one</li><li class=\"d1\">humanity would become <b>like the demons</b> - devil's plot succeeds</li><li class=\"d0\">Mortality given for <b>repentance</b>; cast out = <b>God showing mercy</b></li><li class=\"d1\">a window, an opportunity to repent and return</li><li class=\"d1\">even a refuser could end up where they'd have been originally</li><li class=\"d0\">Death as a <b>gift</b> - opposite of death penalty, opposite of God punishing us today for Adam's disobedience</li><li class=\"d1\">\"didn't say the day you eat I will kill you\" - said <b>you will die</b></li></ul>"},{"t":2325.47,"lv":2,"h":"Two kinds of death","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Q-in-mind: they ate that day and didn't die</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>John of Damascus</b>: <b>physical death</b> (soul/life separated from body) and <b>spiritual death</b> (soul separated from God)</li><li class=\"d0\">Moderns: physical = real, spiritual = analogy/allegory for sin</li><li class=\"d1\">Genesis presents the <b>opposite</b>: real death = <b>life cut off from God</b>; physical is analogous and a <b>result</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>John 17</b>: \"this is life: to know you, the only true God\" - not biological life; biological life an image of it</li><li class=\"d0\">As soon as Adam disobeys, evil enters → <b>spiritual death</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>tourniquet</b> on a finger: tissue necrotizes, gangrene, falls off</li><li class=\"d1\">cut off from God = tourniquet → eventually <b>physically die</b>, return to dust</li><li class=\"d0\">Hope remains; physical death is a <b>consequence of spiritual</b></li></ul>"},{"t":2508.13,"lv":2,"h":"3:24 - Cherubim and the flaming sword","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>3:24</b>: cast out Adam, dwell opposite the garden; <b>cherubim and fiery sword</b> guard the way to the tree of life</li><li class=\"d0\">Cherubim protect <b>where God is</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not because Adam threatens God, but because <b>God's holy presence is a threat to Adam</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Kept from the tree of life <b>for now</b> - it returns at end of <b>Revelation</b>, everyone eating</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Ending on a huge downer\" - <b>worse before it gets better</b> in Genesis</li></ul>"},{"t":2574.57,"lv":2,"h":"Takeaways: the first of three falls","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">First \"fall of humanity\" done; <b>two more</b> in first 11 chapters</li><li class=\"d0\">The word <b>sin</b> has not appeared yet; devil seen, <b>demons</b> not yet</li><li class=\"d0\">This is about <b>death</b> - how death happens</li><li class=\"d0\">Church fathers discuss all three, each emphasizes one</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Irenaeus</b> (2nd c.): <b>Gen 4-9</b>, Cain to the flood</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Eusebius of Caesarea</b> (<i>Demonstration of the Gospel</i>): <b>Gen 10-11</b>, Babel, division of nations</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Augustine</b>: what we just read</li></ul>"},{"t":2702.16,"lv":2,"h":"Augustine and the Latin West","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Problem: Augustine is the <b>only one who writes in Latin</b>; couldn't read anything but Latin</li><li class=\"d1\">West could read only Latin → Western theology built almost entirely on Augustine</li><li class=\"d0\">Western emphasis on <b>\"the fall\"</b> - where everything goes wrong; very <b>freighted</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Augustine's views of <b>justice</b>: death as <b>death penalty</b> - inherited in the West</li><li class=\"d0\">Purpose of Gen 1-3 over three studies: <b>set that aside</b> - not helpful</li></ul>"},{"t":2786.8,"lv":3,"h":"Sin comes in chapter 4; a story of mercy","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Gen 4</b>: start talking about <b>sin</b> - different understanding</li><li class=\"d1\">word hasn't appeared: don't take Adam's breaking a commandment as <b>emblematic sin</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>NT</b> goes to ch. 4 for <b>archetypal sin</b> (next time)</li><li class=\"d0\">This is humanity \"in our youth\" rebelling; world of sin and death is the consequence</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Not</b> a story of God angry at us - <b>at every point merciful toward humanity</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"not really merciful toward the serpent\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Next: sin, maliciousness, evil we do to each other - but not what expulsion is about</li></ul>"},{"t":2896.57,"lv":2,"h":"Q&amp;A: inherited guilt; death as mercy","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Q: you've said we don't inherit <b>Adam's sin</b> - not guilty of what Adam did?</li><li class=\"d1\">\"we're only guilty of our own, which is enough\"</li><li class=\"d1\">nothing in the text says Adam is <b>liable to punishment</b> - death not a penalty; given as <b>mercy</b> so humanity won't be <b>immortal and evil</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Miniseries nobody watched: world where <b>no one could die</b></li><li class=\"d1\">cancer, old-age frailty, pain, injury <b>forever</b> - \"hell on earth\"</li><li class=\"d1\">not how we think, but the reality pointed to here</li></ul>"},{"t":2990.21,"lv":3,"h":"Modern attitudes to death","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Partly from <b>modern life</b> - not that far back in history</li><li class=\"d1\">poor person in 18th-19th c. asked \"live forever like this?\" - <b>no</b></li><li class=\"d1\">we want to because <b>our lives are going okay</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Now when someone dies young or old: all the things they <b>missed</b></li><li class=\"d1\">17th-19th c.: thought of the <b>hardships they were spared</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Out of touch - including <b>technological optimists</b> on verge of <b>abolishing death</b>: \"don't do that\" / \"good luck\"</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Gone really long tonight\" - important chapter</li></ul>"}],"next":"Next: <b>Genesis 4</b> - where <b>sin</b> first appears; the NT's archetypal sin; \"<b>because of you</b>\" wording"});
